   "note": "drawing - `positions` states where the ears bolt, for the Rack Builder. The ears are the flat ends of the panel, so the ear plane is the panel's back face, and the rings stand 88.79 mm in front of it: the side view dimensions 95.00 from the ring tips to the back of the panel's folded edges and 6.21 between the ear plane and the folds, so `at` is 88.79. Of the 95.0 depth, 6.21 stands behind the rail. This states a placement; no dimension changed. The datasheet's \"Mounting Options: Front and Rear Mount\" is a placement too: the rack kit places any part on either face of the rack."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the front view: the panel, five rings end-on 100.0 apart with the middle one on the centre line (41.3 from the left end, estimated), and the four holes midway between them. Each ring stands on a 40 mm bracket across the panel's height, drawn estimated (see `cablmanagerh-panel`). Each hole has a raised collar, 29 mm across outside, drawn as an outline round the open hole. The drawing's inner circle at each collar scales at 21.2 mm. What it means is not stated, so it is an outline ring only. The hole stays the dimensioned 29.0. The rivet is hidden under each ring's base here. The plan view shows none. Not drawn: the fold seen along the front edge of the isometric view (a gap names it)."
  },
  "full-depth": {
